            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Peisistratos</strong><br>\nPeisistratos was born around 600 BC into a noble family in Athens. He was the son of Hippocrates and belonged to a family which claimed descent from the last Athenian king, Codrus. Despite his aristocratic birth, Peisistratos presented himself as a champion of the common people, which helped him gain widespread support. He was known for his intelligence and cunning, as well as his persuasive speaking ability.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Rise to Power</strong><br>\nPeisistratos first attempted to seize power in Athens in 561 BC by exploiting the divisions between the rich and poor. He claimed to be the victim of an attack to gain the sympathy of the masses and won their support. He was initially successful, becoming ruler by appealing to the common people and promising to redistribute land and wealth.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Peisistratos's Tyranny</strong><br>\nOnce in power, Peisistratos maintained control through a mix of charisma, strategic marriages, and military strength. He hired mercenaries to guard him and established a network of loyalists. Although called a tyrant, his rule was generally moderate and focused on the prosperity and expansion of Athens.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
