            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Economic Policies</strong><br>\nUnder Peisistratos's rule, the economy of Athens flourished. He implemented agricultural reforms, encouraged cultivation of olives for export, and supported the arts. This economic boost helped Athens become a powerful and prosperous city-state, setting the foundation for its golden age.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cultural Contributions</strong><br>\nPeisistratos was a patron of the arts and culture. He initiated the construction of many temples and public works. He also started the Panathenaic Festival, which featured athletic competitions and cultural events, contributing to the civic identity of Athens.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Peisistratos's Exiles</strong><br>\nHis rule was interrupted twice when he was ousted from power, but Peisistratos managed to return each time. During his exiles, he gathered support from other regions and used this to his advantage to orchestrate his return. His resilience demonstrated his tenacity and strategic planning skills.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
